  "notes": "Native SSRF checks are kept; a loopback redirect refusal is never bypassed to manufacture a success. Respecting site preferences (robots.txt, Content-Signal, TDMRep) belongs to the engine's site policy (D-identity, ADR-002), not to the transport component: no candidate transport applies it on its own, so this gate blocked every option, the reference included. It was removed from this decision on October 9, 2026 and remains carried by D-identity. The throughput verdict reads only closed-loop runs: under open arrivals, throughput equals the offered rate for any transport that keeps up.",
